**Direct answer:** A concrete break exists – the doctrine‑review logic fails to flag a missing “FOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER” section when no fourth‑shape additions are present. The test *“caps incomplete doctrine evidence with named absences instead of refusing the run”* expects the absence tag `fourth_shape_unclassified`, but the implementation only adds this tag when `fourthShapeCount > 0` (see lines 166‑170 of `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js`). Because the count is zero in the failing case, the tag is never added, causing the test to miss the required absence and the review to be incorrectly marked as having no break.

